I am drinking tea with Prakash at the office.
I tell Prakash about my Friday plans.
"Deepa invited me to her house for dinner," I say.
"That is very good, Maya," Prakash says.
"This is the first time I am going to Deepa's home."
"So I think that I shall buy something for her."
"What should I take?" I ask.
"You can take some local sweets," Prakash says.
"I know a good bakery nearby."
"That is always a good gift," he says.
"Deepa will definitely like it."
He says that good halwa is available at that bakery.
"Then, I shall go there on Friday," I say.
"I will buy a box of halwa for her."
"I shall send the bakery's location on the map," Prakash says.
I thank Prakash very much.
Now I feel very confident about this trip.
